We can solve this problem using a hash table (dictionary in Python) to store the frequency of each character in the string. We iterate through the string and for each character, we check if its frequency is even or odd. If it's even, we remove the character and continue to the next character. If it's odd, we add the character to the hash table and continue to the next character. We repeat this process until we reach the end of the string.

